From db982a01a32975fe3c640acefa3d5b7dd8e78d9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Linh Nguyen Van <29197556+nguyenvanlinh14@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:35:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(e2e): use web-first URL assertions in logout spec

After the mocked /user/logout redirect, the spec waited with
page.waitForURL('/provider') and then read the URL once with
expect(page.url()).toContain('/provider'). The second step is a
point-in-time read of a plain string: it cannot retry, and it is
weaker than needed because toContain also matches e.g. '/provider-foo'.

Replace both with a single `await expect(page).toHaveURL('/provider')`,
which auto-waits and retries until the URL matches (or the expect
timeout elapses) and compares the whole URL. The test still verifies
the same thing: logging out ends on /provider.

The request.url() check on the awaited waitForRequest() result is left
as is: it reads a value from an already resolved Request, so there is
no race, and there is no web-first matcher for it.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
Signed-off-by: Linh Nguyen Van <29197556+nguyenvanlinh14@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 ui/tests/e2e/logout.spec.ts | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/tests/e2e/logout.spec.ts b/ui/tests/e2e/logout.spec.ts
index aaeae8690..464a83f34 100644
--- a/ui/tests/e2e/logout.spec.ts
+++ b/ui/tests/e2e/logout.spec.ts
@@ -26,7 +26,6 @@ test.describe('Logout Page Tests', () => {
     const request = await waitForLogoutRequest;
     expect(request.url()).toContain('/user/logout');
 
-    await page.waitForURL('/provider');
-    expect(page.url()).toContain(`/provider`);
+    await expect(page).toHaveURL('/provider');
   });
 });
